/*
 * NT35596 FHD video-mode panel, Tianma module - Redmi Note 4 MTK ("nikel")
 *
 * Ported to the MT6797 3.18 LCM framework (SHIFTPHONES android_kernel_shift_mt6797).
 *
 * Origin: Xiaomi, MiCode/Xiaomi_Kernel_OpenSource branch hennessy-l-oss,
 *         drivers/misc/mediatek/lcm/nt35596_fhd_dsi_vdo_tianma/ (Redmi Note 2/3, 3.10)
 *
 * Verified against nikel's stock kernel (Xiaomi 3.18.M2+, 2019-04-19):
 *  - lcm_initialization_setting and lcm_cabc_on_initialization_setting compile
 *    byte-identical to the stock tables only WITH TE_ENABLE_FUNCTION defined
 *    (498 rows each). Do not edit these tables.
 *  - lcm_suspend_setting and lcm_backlight_level_setting below are nikel's
 *    versions read from the stock binary (they differ from the Note 2 source).
 *
 * Changes from the 3.10 source:
 *  - legacy mt_set_gpio_* / hard-coded GPIO numbers replaced by this driver's
 *    own pinctrl states (node "xiaomi,nikel-lcm-gpio" in nikel.dts), for
 *    reset, bias ENP/ENN and backlight enable - see the comment further down
 *  - TPS65132 bias chip bound through DT (compatible "mediatek,i2c_lcd_bias",
 *    i2c0 @ 0x3e) instead of i2c_register_board_info
 *  - KTD3116 low-brightness bit-bang (levels < 32) left out for the first boot:
 *    it needs microsecond GPIO timing, which pinctrl state switching cannot
 *    guarantee. Brightness below 32 is clamped to 32 until it is re-added.
 *  - compare_id: LK already picks the panel (lcm=1-nt35596_fhd_tianma_phantom);
 *    the kernel side only checks the NT35596 chip ID, not Xiaomi's ID pins.
 *  - LK-only code removed (this file is kernel-only).
 */

